    "english":  "The mountain pools, once dry and fearful, now brim with clear water;\nroaring cascades plunge down the high mountain slopes.\nThe forest stream, tumbling heavy rocks in its torrential surge,\nswallows the bamboo clumps along the bank and dashes against the trees.\nWith deep, resonant thunder the dark rainclouds flash their lightning,\npromising showers upon the parched woods.\nLook, dear friend! In this dried sandalwood forest where the elephant,\nhaving fed on white bamboo grain, sleeps peacefully upon the fragrant slope,\nthe skies have heralded the rainsΓÇö\nhe who went to seek wealth will surely return now to claim your hand!",
